The RTC alarm callback test does not clear the alarm pending status between test iterations. If an RTC driver implementation does not trigger a callback when the alarm is already pending, the test will fail on the second iteration.

The fix is to restructure the test to be consistent with `test_alarm.c`, where the RTC time is set and the alarm pending status is cleared at the beginning of each test iteration. This ensures each test iteration starts from a clean state, making the test more robust.

